VenusOS-TankSensor — DIY Tank Level Sensor for Venus OS

Uses an ADS1115 16-bit I2C ADC to read a resistive tank sender
(e.g. Osculati 10-180 ohm) and publish the tank level on D-Bus.

The tank appears in Venus OS GUI (v1 and v2), Remote Console, and VRM.

Hardware required:
  - ADS1115 breakout board (I2C, ~4 EUR)
  - Resistive tank sender (10-180 ohm European standard)
  - 100 ohm reference resistor
  - 4 wires to RPi GPIO (3.3V, GND, SDA, SCL)

Configuration:
  Edit /data/dbus-tank-ads1115/tank-sensor.conf after installation.

Testing without hardware:
  1. The service starts in --simulate mode by default
  2. Run: python3 /data/dbus-tank-ads1115/test_tank_sim.py 50
     to set the tank level to 50%
  3. Or: python3 /data/dbus-tank-ads1115/test_tank_sim.py ramp
     for automatic 0-100-0 cycling

Switching to real hardware:
  Edit services/dbus-tank-ads1115/run and remove --simulate flag.
